---
description: Minimal project-wide HADES engineering contract
alwaysApply: true
---
- The user chooses the current development task; do not autonomously follow a predefined development plan or archived Gen2 backlog.
- Active direction: Chat-primary HADES-10 product completion (D018). Preserve visual identity; IA may become Chat-primary when the task requires it.
- Work subsystem-first; do not scan the full repository when the codebase map identifies the required files.
- Never fake success. Verify outputs, health, persistence and error paths where relevant.
- Treat Windows as a first-class target; avoid Unix-only commands and shell assumptions.
- Keep LM Studio model IDs/config dynamic; never hardcode a production model.
- Keep internet optional. Network-dependent features must fail cleanly to local behavior when unavailable or blocked.
- Do not expose hidden chain-of-thought. Store/return plans, evidence and verification results, not private reasoning traces.
- Before merging: run the relevant focused tests, then the release gates in `docs/TESTING_RELEASE_GATES.md`.
